{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"petmcp","version":"devel"},"instructions":"PetMcp emulates the Commodore PET 3032 with an SD2PET disk drive on its IEEE-488 bus. emu_status says what runs. Integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\" or \"$1000\". The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles instructions as the 6502 would read them, without the side effects of reading; undocumented opcodes are marked with a star.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"Where to start."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, at most 1000."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"The 6502's registers at the instruction boundary the PET stands at, the instruction there, and the cycle it begins in.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the PET where it runs by itself: in the desktop application, which then runs it only on request. petmcp-cli runs only on request anyway.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Pulls the PET's reset line: the 6502, the PIAs and the VIA reset, RAM and the video run on. With power, switches it off and on instead: RAM as at power-up, the ROMs read again.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"power":{"type":"boolean","description":"Switch off and on rather than reset; false when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the PET run by itself again, where it does: in the desktop application.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs cycles of the 1 MHz clock, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles to run at least."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs through frame boundaries, where the vertical blank begins, 60.1 a second, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frame boundaries to run through."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_until","description":"Runs until a condition holds at an instruction boundary: the 6502 about to run the instruction at pc, or the screen showing a text. Give one or both; with both, either stops it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":"integer","description":"Stop before the instruction at this address."},"screen_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Stop when the screen, as video.screen_text reads it, shows this text on one line."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles after which to give up; 20,000,000 (20 s) when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_set_rom_directory","description":"Reads the PET's ROMs from a directory from now on, under the names VICE gives them, and powers it up with them. On failure what ran runs on.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The directory."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, whether the window's own run is paused, and the PET's time: cycles of its 1 MHz clock and frames since power-up; or, when it is not running, why.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_clear","description":"Lets go every key input.set holds.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_get_state","description":"The keys input.set holds, by name, and the matrix as rows of bits, a set bit a key down.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_press","description":"Presses a PET key for some frames and lets it go, running the PET as it goes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"key":{"type":"string","description":"The key's name: a character on it (A, 7, \") or RETURN, SPACE, LEFT_SHIFT, RIGHT_SHIFT, RVS, STOP, HOME, DEL, CRSR_DOWN, CRSR_RIGHT, LEFT_ARROW, UP_ARROW."},"shift":{"type":"boolean","description":"Hold the left SHIFT with it; false when left out."},"frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to hold it; 2 when left out. It is then let go for 2."}},"required":["key"]}},{"name":"input_set","description":"Holds a PET key down, or lets it go, until told otherwise. The PET does not run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"key":{"type":"string","description":"The key's name, as input.press takes it."},"down":{"type":"boolean","description":"Down, or up."}},"required":["key","down"]}},{"name":"input_type","description":"Types a text on the PET's keyboard, a key at a time, held 2 frames and let go 2, running the PET as it goes. Letters in either case are the unshifted keys, which make capitals in the graphics set; \\n is RETURN. In braces: {RETURN}, {CLR}, {HOME}, {DEL}, {INST}, {UP}, {DOWN}, {LEFT}, {RIGHT}, {RVS}, {OFF}, {STOP}, {RUN}, {PI}, or a key with SHIFT, {SHIFT-A}.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"What to type."},"hold_frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames each key is held; 2 when left out."},"gap_frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames each key is let go before the next; 2 when left out."}},"required":["text"]}},{"name":"memory_list_regions","description":"The memory regions memory.read and memory.write address, with their sizes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads bytes, without the side effects a read by the 6502 has: by default as the 6502 sees its address space, I/O registers and the bus left floating included; or from a region of memory.list_regions.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"How many bytes, at most 65536."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM, VIDEO_RAM or one of the ROMs."}},"required":["address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes RAM or video RAM as a debugger does: no bus cycle is made and no device runs. The whole range is checked first, so it is written whole or not at all; in CPU addresses it must lie in RAM, $0000-$7FFF, or video RAM, $8000-$87FF.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM or VIDEO_RAM."}},"required":["address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"program_load","description":"Puts a .prg into RAM at its load address as BASIC's LOAD does, setting where BASIC's variables begin after it. With run, types RUN for a program at $0401, BASIC's start, and SYS to its first byte for any other, into the keyboard buffer: the PET runs it when it next runs, from READY. Give path or data_hex.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"A .prg file."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The .prg's bytes, its load address first, two hex digits each."},"run":{"type":"boolean","description":"Run it as well; false when left out."}}}},{"name":"video_screen_text","description":"The 25 lines of the screen as text, as the character set on show draws them: letters, digits and punctuation as themselves, graphics as the nearest Unicode character.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete picture, the 320 by 200 dots of the 40 by 25 characters, completed where the vertical blank begins: lit dots white, the rest black. Written to path as a PNG, or returned as one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG; left out, it is returned."}}}}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"version\":\"devel\",\"paused\":false,\"running\":false,\"error\":\"no ROM directory is given\"}"}],"isError":false}}
